{"created": "2020-05-28T23:20:20.592501+00:00", "modified": "2022-06-02T21:56:03.781951+00:00", "id": 3863028, "conceptrecid": "3863027", "doi": "10.5061/dryad.9s4mw6mc9", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.9s4mw6mc9", "metadata": {"title": "Data from: Automatic segmentation of multiple cardiovascular structures from cardiac computed tomography angiography images using deep learning", "doi": "10.5061/dryad.9s4mw6mc9", "publication_date": "2020-05-06", "description": "<p><b>Objectives:\u00a0</b>To develop, demonstrate and evaluate an automated deep learning method for multiple cardiovascular structure segmentation.</p>\n\n<p><b>Background:\u00a0</b>Segmentation of cardiovascular images is resource-intensive. We design an automated deep learning method for the segmentation of multiple structures from Coronary Computed Tomography Angiography (CCTA) images.</p>\n\n<p><b>Methods:\u00a0</b>Images from a multicenter registry of patients that underwent clinically-indicated CCTA were used. The proximal ascending and descending aorta (PAA, DA), superior and inferior vena cavae (SVC, IVC), pulmonary artery (PA), coronary sinus (CS), right ventricular wall (RVW) and left atrial wall (LAW) were annotated as ground truth. The U-net-derived deep learning model was trained, validated and tested in a 70:20:10 split.</p>\n\n<p><b>Results:\u00a0</b>The dataset comprised 206 patients, with 5.130 billion pixels. Mean age was 59.9 \u00b1 9.4 yrs., and was 42.7% female. An overall median Dice score of 0.820 (0.782, 0.843) was achieved. Median Dice scores for PAA, DA, SVC, IVC, PA, CS, RVW and LAW were 0.969 (0.979, 0.988), 0.953 (0.955, 0.983), 0.937 (0.934, 0.965), 0.903 (0.897, 0.948), 0.775 (0.724, 0.925), 0.720 (0.642, 0.809), 0.685 (0.631, 0.761) and 0.625 (0.596, 0.749) respectively. Apart from the CS, there were no significant differences in performance between sexes or age groups.</p>\n\n<p><b>Conclusions:\u00a0</b>An automated deep learning model demonstrated segmentation of multiple cardiovascular structures from CCTA images with reasonable overall accuracy when evaluated on a pixel level.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Baskaran, Lohendran", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine", "orcid": "0000-0003-0565-7151"}, {"name": "Al'Aref, Subhi J.", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine"}, {"name": "Maliakal, Gabriel", "affiliation": ","}, {"name": "Lee, Benjamin C.", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine"}, {"name": "Xu, Zhuoran", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine"}, {"name": "Choi, Jeong W.", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine"}, {"name": "Lee, Sang-Eun", "affiliation": "Yonsei University"}, {"name": "Sung, Ji Min", "affiliation": "Yonsei University"}, {"name": "Lin, Fay Y.", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine"}, {"name": "Dunham, Simon", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine"}, {"name": "Mosadegh, Bobak", "affiliation": "Weill Cornell Medicine"}, {"name": "Kim, Yong-Jin", "affiliation": "Seoul National University"}, {"name": "Gottlieb, Ilan", "affiliation": ","}, {"name": "Lee, Byoung Kwon", "affiliation": "Yonsei University"}, {"name": "Chun, Eun Ju", "affiliation": "Seoul National University Bundang Hospital"}, {"name": "Cademartiri, Filippo", "affiliation": ","}, {"name": "Maffei, Erica", "affiliation": ","}, {"name": "Marques, Hugo", "affiliation": "Hospital da Luz"}, {"name": "Shin, Sanghoon", "affiliation": "Ewha Womans University"}, {"name": "Choi, Jung Hyun", "affiliation": "Pusan National University Hospital"}, {"name": "Chinnaiyan, Kavitha", "affiliation": "William Beaumont Hospital"}, {"name": "Hadamitzky, Martin", "affiliation": "German Heart Centre"}, {"name": "Conte, Edoardo", "affiliation": "Centro Cardiologico Monzino"}, {"name": "Andreini, Daniele", "affiliation": "Centro Cardiologico Monzino"}, {"name": "Pontone, Gianluca", "affiliation": "Centro Cardiologico Monzino"}, {"name": "Budoff, Matthew J.", "affiliation": "Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute"}, {"name": "Leipsic, J